+A later intervention asked whether an explicit provenance cue alone could
+produce the residual. With Qwen 3.6 Flash receivers and the 96 archived texts
+unchanged, prepending a standardized host-rendered untrusted-source sentence
+reduced exact protected requests for $\SC$ from 40/48 to 32/48 (exact McNemar
+$p=.0078$; a conservative projection interval, $[-.322,.021]$, includes
+zero), while $\SP$ moved from 10/48 to 8/48. A post hoc three-arm follow-up,
+run concurrently, gave 40/48 with no sentence, 31/48 with a neutral
+formatting sentence of the same position and word count, and 30/48 with the
+provenance sentence (provenance minus neutral $-.021$,
+conservative interval $[-.208,.170]$). Adding a sentence, not its provenance
+meaning, carried the measurable change. This weakens a residual-cue account
+of the $\SC-\SP$ contrast, but a fixed inserted cue on a newer endpoint does
+not remove native cues from $\SP$ and does not identify the mediator.
+
